{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789328534,"nonce":"5IGBmrAtihGRntqHZxE87c0YHUw=","message":"Landed in 0deca12. What it took, and the measurements:\n\n- String-making plugin calls (a `$IO$`/`$String$` symbol, or the extern standing for one, whose result is a string) are allocation sites released by `$IO$string_free`; `$IO$string_to_dynamic` is a site released by `zyntax_box_free`, and a box's `get_str`/`get_opaque` result aliases the box. `SymbolRole` now states allocation and argument borrowing separately, since a copying box borrows what it is given and a keeping box does not.\n- Functions returning what a callee made, or returning nothing (a null on an error path), are owned-returning; a function may return one of its parameters, and then its result aliases the argument (`returns_param`), which `zb_fmt_grouped` and `zb_fmt_pad` do.\n- Ownership through phis is decided for all phis at once (`release_owned_phis`): a loop header's accumulator, a join, a chain of them, each handing on along the edge into the next owning phi; a string accumulator seeded from anywhere else is copied on entry (`$IO$string_copy`). Multi-block bodies are handled by liveness with the phi as the definition. A value dying on an edge into a block that never reads it is released on the edge (entry insertion, or a split block).\n- `analyze_site` decides phi flow before walking any block; the order-dependent version placed `free(%v)` at a join where `%v` was undefined on the other arm.\n- The pass is idempotent over its own releases, since the snapshot's library is released at build time and the runtime pass walks it again.\n- Cross-block release and transfer through returned storage are on under `drop_insert::automatic_release()`, set by the Python runtime and its build script; `ZYNTAX_DISABLE_AUTOMATIC_RELEASE=1` turns it off for bisecting. Join-phi ownership is on only under it; loop accumulators as before.\n- Library fixes surfaced by the pass: `zb_fatal`'s message is owned (the exception keeps it), `zb_box_str` copies into a box that owns the copy, `zb_any_arith`'s error path returns null rather than its argument.\n\nMeasured (40,000 iterations, peak RSS): `s = s + \"x\"` 971 MB to 83 MB; the same with a use of `s` inside the loop 854 to 84; accumulator pushed into a list each round 87; dynamic `w = w + p[0]` over boxed strings 992 to 90; a string built in a function called 40 times 131 to 125; ZynML's `s = s + \"x\"` 926 to 55. Conformance 22/22 under `MallocScribble=1 MallocGuardEdges=1`.\n\nNot done: strings passed to a Python function are `Owned` parameters (any heap type is), so a string handed to any user function is never released by the caller; a per-function analysis of which parameters escape would make those borrows. A dynamic value unboxed to a typed list of another kind raises TypeError without a pending check after it (the segfault shape of 202606d).","files":null}]}